From 5ba97f31bcb646be8e73f8964ce643a06a4c32c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 08:43:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bmips: introduce bcma support for integrated Wlan in SoC

adapt fallback-sprom to support loading a fallback sprom for the specific dt node.
adapt bcm6362.dtsi to map the wlan node
adapt other.mk to support building 6362 wlan as part of bcma
introduce CONFIG_BCMA_HOST_SOC_BRCM6362_WLAN to build the wlan 6362 host driver

Most of this sent upstream at https://lore.kernel.org/linux-devicetree/20260529-add-bcm6362-wlan-v1-0-722242777f58@gmail.com/T.
Will update if someone upstream ask for changes.

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
